    choose: [['Kai must prepare (for / into) a bigger stage.', 'for'], ['Luis will coordinate (with / from) the festival team.', 'with'], ['Let’s clarify who handles (what / whose).', 'what'], ['We can turn the opportunity (into / under) a plan.', 'into'], ['A large audience is (expected / expecting).', 'expected'], ['The meeting is six weeks (before / during) the festival.', 'before']],
    choices: [['Which stage arrangement is confirmed?', 'Kai will perform on one of the main stages.', 'Kai has already completed the festival.', 'A'], ['What does the audience statement describe?', 'An exact count of future ticket sales.', 'A large live audience and online viewers are expected.', 'B'], ['What should Luis do?', 'Coordinate with the festival’s video team.', 'Assume there is no event video team.', 'A'], ['What remains ahead?', 'The production meeting.', 'Rehearsals and the actual performance.', 'B']],
    mission: { situation: 'You are Maya. Your tutor is Mr. Shibata. The festival is six weeks away. Kai has a main-stage performance with live and online audiences expected. The festival provides video production, and Luis can coordinate with its team.', task: 'Clarify responsibilities, identify preparation priorities, and explain the opportunity without guaranteeing a result.', roles: ['Mr. Shibata', 'Maya'], lines: ['Maya, what does your team need to prepare for this larger stage?', 'What would you like to clarify about video production?', 'How could Luis coordinate with the festival team?', 'What other rehearsal or technical work matters?', 'What could the event offer Kai without guaranteeing his future?'], evidence: 'Six weeks before fictional festival. One main stage, substantial expected live and online audience, festival video team with Luis coordination. No exact attendance, stage name, stream platform, fee or technical rider supplied. Song inclusion is still to be negotiated next episode. Do not turn preparation into an already completed performance or guaranteed popularity.', useful: ['We need to prepare for ...', 'Who will handle ...?', 'Luis can coordinate with ...', 'Our first priorities are ...', 'This could introduce Kai to ...'] },
